---
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
import Avatar from '../components/Avatar.astro';
---
<PageLayout title="About" lead={`Why ${site.name} exists and how articles are checked.`}>
  <div class="not-prose mb-8 flex items-center gap-5">
    <Avatar size={96} />
    <div>
      <p class="m-0 text-xl font-semibold">{site.author.name}</p>
      <p class="m-0 text-muted">Software engineer in Berlin, 20+ years in the industry</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <p>
    I'm a software engineer with more than 20 years of experience, most of it spent designing software systems. I work
    full time for a company at the moment, and I have taken on freelance projects alongside it in the past. I plan to do
    more.
  </p>
  <p>
    Every time I looked into freelancing in Germany, the answers were spread across law texts, tax office leaflets,
    insurer websites and forum threads, mostly in German and often out of date. This site puts them in one place, in
    plain English: what you have to do, in which order, and what it costs.
  </p>
  <p>
    I'm not a tax advisor or an insurance broker. That's why every article is built on primary sources and lists them,
    and why the articles say clearly when your situation needs professional advice.
  </p>
  <p>
    Outside work, I'm married with one child. I play bass guitar, play World of Warcraft casually, and breed tropical
    fish.
  </p>
  <h2>How articles are checked</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Every figure comes from an official source: the tax office, public insurers, the pension fund or the law itself.</li>
    <li>Every article shows the date it was last checked. Rates and thresholds are reviewed every January.</li>
    <li>This is general information, not advice. For your own situation, talk to a tax advisor or licensed insurance broker.</li>
    <li>
      I do my best to verify everything, but laws, rates and office practice change, and mistakes can happen. You are
      responsible for checking the details that matter to you against the official sources (each article links them)
      before you act on them.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <h2>Found a mistake?</h2>
  <p>Please <a href="/contact">tell me</a>. Corrections are fixed quickly and noted in the article.</p>
</PageLayout>
